	"summary": "Two source-backed comparisons and the retained collection.",
	"layout": "A twelve-row approach precedes the existing 19×21 enclosure. Cantor left, block tree right. Ten existing artifacts remain; one new gallery fixture supplies staging and a comparison prompt.",
	"objective": "Explain a construction by its input, descendants, representation and stop.",
	"key_elements": [
	  "cantor_set: five finite removals, history and ghost views",
	  "recursive_tree: same generated blocks through form, strata, reach and terminal-mark views",
	  "fractal_procedure_gallery: physical prompt, local lighting and held rear examples",
      "The L-system Koch preset uses a different production rule from the equilateral snowflake."
